prompt:
You are a compliance referee. Explain this cross-department gap to a launch manager in 2-3 plain sentences and give 2-3 concrete fix options. Use ONLY these facts; do not invent any.
Seam type: support_capacity_gap
Title: Promised 336 staffed hours/week but staffing covers 240; Support hiring frozen until 2027-03-31
Departments: Finance, HR, Legal
Facts: {"agents": 6, "budget_coverage": ["B-001 Support staff (6 FTE): Business hours Mon-Fri 08:00-18:00; no out-of-hours line"], "gap_hours": 96.0, "hiring_frozen_until": "2027-03-31", "promise": "Premium customers receive 24x7 support, with at least two agents staffed at all times and a first response within 15 minutes for payment failures.", "required_hours_per_week": 336.0, "staffed_hours_per_week": 240.0}
Return JSON: {"explanation": str, "fix_options": [str]}

response:
```json
{
  "explanation": "The promise to Premium customers requires 336 staffed agent-hours per week (24x7 support, at least two agents at all times, and a 15-minute first response for payment failures), but the 6 budgeted support staff provide only 240 hours, leaving a 96-hour weekly gap. The budget line (B-001) covers only business hours, Mon-Fri 08:00-18:00, with no out-of-hours line, so nights and weekends have no coverage at all. HR cannot close the gap by hiring because Support hiring is frozen until 2027-03-31.",
  "fix_options": [
    "Legal revises the Premium promise to match funded coverage (business hours Mon-Fri 08:00-18:00) and removes or rescopes the 24x7, two-agent, and 15-minute payment-failure commitments before launch.",
    "Finance funds an out-of-hours support line, and HR seeks an exception to the hiring freeze, to cover the 96-hour weekly gap, including nights and weekends.",
    "Delay the 24x7 Premium commitment until Support hiring reopens after 2027-03-31, and launch now with only the support terms the current 6-agent staffing can meet."
  ]
}
```
